  "source_evidence": [
    "Asterinas pinned kernel/core/src/net/socket/unix/ctrl_msg.rs:130-148 writes a four-entry header, installs each FD and then copies its number.",
    "kernel/core/src/net/socket/util/message_header.rs:109-118 breaks on the third copy failure before adding this cmsg to reported length.",
    "Linux reference net/core/scm.c:348-370 builds and reports the two-delivery prefix header after the loop. The complete earlier entries remain installed."
  ],
  "impact": "The raw first two FD numbers remain valid, but zero reported control length omits their prefix and the third unpublished descriptor also remains installed. Whole-receive rollback would incorrectly revoke the legitimate prefix."
}
